### Commandline Options
# These commandline options are available when launching the game executable.
# Options can be combined where they make sense. Argument values can be surrounded by double quotes.

##### NOTE: All of these are developer features! Use at your own risk. #####

### Game-start related

# Skip the startup screen and jump directly into the game, loading history
-skip

# Play as the ruler for the indicated title key (example: e_byzantium)
-play=<title_name>

# Select a specific bookmark to start at. Mainly important for start-year. (example: bm_867_carolingians)
-bookmark=<bookmark_name>

# Load and continue with the last savegame
-continuelastsave

# Load the specific savegame by name
-loadsave=<name>

### Multiplayer related

# Auto-start an MP server with a specific name
-host_server=<name>

# Auto-join an MP server with a specific name
-join_server=<name>

# Set the default server password (for hosting or joining)
-server_password=<password>

# Number of players required to auto-start the game
-auto_run_num_players=<number>

# Number of seconds to delay auto-starting a game when players are present
-auto_run_start_delay_sec=<number>

# Auto-accept anyone joining an MP game
-hotjoinautoaccept

### More specialist options - useful for modding

# Start the game with "debug" aka "developer" mode on (enabled by default for debug builds)
-debug_mode

# Skip calculating the checksum for local files. This will speed up startup slightly, but make multiplayer not work.
-skip_checksum

# Start the game with a specific random seed. (every new game started will have this random seed)
-random_seed=<number>

# Change the default random number generator seed for the character designer (get consistently same start character)
-designer_seed=<number>

# Do not auto-open the error log file on game startup when in debug mode
-suppress_error_log

# Disable in-game encyclopedia, can make for faster startup/reload times during development
-disable_encyclopedia

### Advanced / Tech options - use with care

# Load database in threaded mode during startup. (default: yes)
-load_databases_threaded=yes/no

# Change the name of the window (useful when running multiple instances of the game)
-window_title=<text>

# Change the number of task threads used (overrides the automatic calculation)
-taskthreads=<number>

# Change the number of low-prio task threads used (overrides the automatic calculation)
-lowtaskthreads=<number>

# Change the default memory allocation for the virtual file system in MBs (overrides automatic calculation)
-io_memory_mb=<number>

# Specify a different output directory for the crash reporter (instead of <user_dir>/crash_reporter/
-crash_reporter_dir=<directory>

# Prefix all log files with a specific text. (useful for certain types of comparative debugging / MP testing)
-logprefix=<prefix>
# Postfix all log files with a specific text. (useful for certain types of comparative debugging / MP testing)
-logpostfix=<postfix>

# Start with specific graphics backend
-opengl
-dx11
-vulkan
# Pick a random graphics backend out of the available ones
-randomrenderer

# Log framerate data to 'logs/framerate.tsv' file
-log_framerate

# Log additional Audio debug info
-audiodebug

# Debug camera controller (disables gamepad cursors/navigation)
-debug_controller_camera

# Enable gamepad controller input (default enabled, except on Linux, where there were issues with some controllers)
-handle_controller_input

# Enable IO stats
-io_stats

# Enable Memory stats
-memory_stats

# Disable shader cache loading from file-system
-gfxdebug_disable_shadercache

# Log additional texture-streaming data to debug.log
-gfx_texture_streamer_info

# Enable extended checks for 3D mesh asset loading
-extended_mesh_checks

# Enable the experimental script optimizer
-script_optimizer

# Enables checksum calculation each game tick even if off normally, such as during single player.
-checksum_always_update

### Commandline Action Meta functions

# Print registered commandline Option & Actions (not all commandline options are registered properly :P)
-command_line_help

# Runs the specified in-game console command, then exits. (init state: main - very early)
-run_console_action_main=<console_command>

# Runs the specified in-game console command, then exits. (init state: clausewitz - engine initialized)
-run_console_action_clausewitz=<console_command>

# Runs the specified in-game console command, then exits. (init state: application - game initialized)
-run_console_action=<console_command>

# Show the help for the built-in "image analyzer" tool. Run to see how to use this tool and its options.
-image_analyzer

### Automated testing

# Start an automated test
-automated_test

# Make an automatic save-game every X years (for hands-off testing)
-save_every=<years>

# Directly load into a daily save (looks for save file named "Daily_<year>_<month>_<day>.ck3" of current day)
-load_daily_save

# Run in 'no graphics' mode. Useful for fully automated tests.
-nographics

# Stop the game after history setup (and open error log if not empty)
-shutdown_after_history

# Disable AI activity (same as console command 'AI.Enabled')
-disable_ai

### Authentication / Account login

# Session token passed in from PDX launcher
-pdx-launcher-session-token=<token>

